      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmmmm, hardening is certainly enabled or `ITypArrayDeathTest.OutOfBounds` would be failing. But there are various options so maybe hardened iterators are not. I don\u0027t even know for sure if they\u0027re enabled in chromium, I guess I just assumed because `std::ranges::copy` is supposedly safe.\n\nYou should be able to check the values of the config macros to see what config you\u0027re getting in various build setups:\n\n- iterator hardening options: `_LIBCPP_ABI_BOUNDED_ITERATORS` etc. These change the ABI so the hardening level doesn\u0027t affect them. https://libcxx.llvm.org/Hardening.html#abi-options\n\nNot relevant here but fyi:\n\n- libc++ hardening level: `_LIBCPP_HARDENING_MODE` https://libcxx.llvm.org/Hardening.html#notes-for-users\n- absl hardening level: `ABSL_OPTION_HARDENED` https://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp/blob/fc1384e6f098c9861b106e55526d6504fc5561e4/absl/base/options.h#L156",
